<header><h1>Agenda Phase: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_agenda_phase">Agenda Phase</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Rules Reference</h2>
    <ul>
    <li>(Thunder&rsquo;s Edge) A space station cannot be elected, although its influence can be used to cast votes.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can you vote using the influence from Trade stations? A: Yes, Space Stations are used for voting but may not be elected.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ul>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When a player casts votes during the agenda phase, it is not that player&rsquo;s turn for the purpose of game effects.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When do &lsquo;at the start of your turn&rsquo; abilities happen, and do they work in other phases?&rdquo;: &ldquo;They only exist in the action phase: you don&rsquo;t have turns in the strategy, status or agenda phases.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may cast votes with <a href="/R_space_stations">space stations</a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Thunder's_Edge:~:text=The%20Triad"><i>The Triad</i></a>, and the <a href="/F_deepwrought">Deepwrought</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="/F_deepwrought#oceanbound">ocean cards</a>.<sup>6,9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, &ldquo;Voting with Space Stations&rdquo;: &ldquo;can you vote with space stations, oceans, and the triad? &hellip; A: Yeah you can vote with them.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, Space Stations: &ldquo;Space Stations are used for voting but may not be elected.&rdquo; Relics: &ldquo;Q: Can you vote using The Triad relic? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Players may exhaust planets during the agenda phase for purposes other than casting votes, such as spending resources or using technology specialties. Planets exhausted this way cannot then be used to cast votes.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I exhaust planets for resources or technology specialties during the agenda phase?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; nothing limits planets to voting then. You can spend them on things like Inheritance Systems or research from a Technology Rider, but those planets then can&rsquo;t vote.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Casting zero votes for an outcome is the same as abstaining. A player that casts zero votes gains no positive or negative effects of voting for that outcome.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ, Agendas: &ldquo;A vote of zero is the same as abstaining; that player gains no positive or negative effects of voting &lsquo;For&rsquo; or &lsquo;Against&rsquo; on an agenda if they contributed zero votes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I abstain, and does casting zero votes let me use Distinguished Councilor or Bribery?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Casting zero votes is the same as abstaining.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Consider zero votes to be mechanically the same as abstaining.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The speaker decides tied outcomes even if they cannot vote on that agenda, such as when they are the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player or have played a rider, as deciding a tie is not a vote.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can a speaker who can&rsquo;t vote, such as the Nekro Virus or a speaker who played a rider, still break ties?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; breaking a tie isn&rsquo;t voting, so the speaker always does it.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 8.19: &ldquo;If there is a tie &hellip; the speaker decides which of the tied outcomes to resolve.&rdquo; No exception for a speaker who cannot vote.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>An agenda&rsquo;s outcome affects every player, regardless of how they voted or whether they abstained, unless the agenda states otherwise, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Mutiny"><i>Mutiny</i></a> agenda.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does an agenda&rsquo;s outcome affect everyone, or only the players who voted for it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Everyone, unless the card itself limits the effect to players who voted a certain way, as Mutiny does. Abstaining doesn&rsquo;t exempt you.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>During the agenda phase, if the outcome of an agenda affects multiple players, it does so in speaker order, starting with the <a href="/R_speaker">speaker</a> and proceeding clockwise. If an agenda is resolved during the action phase, such as with the <a href="/F_keleres">Keleres</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Thunder's_Edge_2:~:text=Executive%20Order"><i>Executive Order</i></a> technology, it does so in <a href="/R_initiative_order">initiative order</a>.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;In what order are agenda-phase secret objectives scored?&rdquo;: &ldquo;In speaker order, clockwise; it only matters if several players would win from the points, a tie that also goes clockwise from the speaker.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling (Xxcha hero resolving agendas during the action phase): &ldquo;Initiative order determines the winner. Initiative order is always the lowest initiative player onwards, regardless of who the active player is.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Riders are resolved after the agenda is fully resolved, in speaker order.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When an agenda outcome and a rider both award points, which resolves first?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The agenda&rsquo;s outcome resolves first, then the riders that predicted it.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 8.22b: &ldquo;After resolving the outcome of the agenda, any abilities that were dependent upon predicting the outcome are resolved.&rdquo; LRR 1.20 gives speaker order for simultaneous abilities in the agenda phase.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player successfully predicts multiple riders, they resolve one at a time, in the order that player chooses, with each other player having the opportunity to resolve an ability between each.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 1.20: players &ldquo;take turns resolving abilities starting with the speaker and proceeding clockwise. This process continues until each player has resolved each ability that they wish to resolve during that window.&rdquo; Turn-taking implies one at a time. No source states that the player chooses the order.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Each pair of players may resolve one transaction during each agenda.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 94.6: &ldquo;While resolving each agenda during the agenda phase, a player may perform one transaction with each other player.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can players make transactions with non-neighbors during the agenda phase?&rdquo;: &ldquo;while each agenda is being resolved &hellip; every pair of players may make one transaction, neighbors or not.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play p. 20: &ldquo;Each player may negotiate up to one transaction with each other player while resolving the vote for each agenda.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Planets are readied at the end of the agenda phase; other exhausted cards, such as technologies and agents, stay exhausted.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I exhaust planets for resources or technology specialties during the agenda phase?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Exhausted cards other than planets don&rsquo;t ready at the end of the agenda phase.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 8.4: &ldquo;Step 3&mdash;Ready Planets: Each player readies each of their exhausted planets.&rdquo; Names only planets.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, Ready Planets: &ldquo;Each player readies all of their planet cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Deepwrought player&rsquo;s <a href="/F_deepwrought#oceanbound">ocean cards</a>, <a href="/R_space_stations">space stations</a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Thunder's_Edge:~:text=The%20Triad"><i>The Triad</i></a> are also readied at the end of the agenda phase.<sup>3,6,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play p. 21, Agenda Phase, &ldquo;3. READY PLANETS&rdquo;: &ldquo;Each player readies all of their planet cards.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, Deepwrought Scholarate: &ldquo;What do Ocean Cards do? A: They are planet cards and can be spent as such.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 10: &ldquo;Each space station has a corresponding planet card, which is gained exhausted and is spent, readied as if it were a planet.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> The Triad card text (not a numbered source): &ldquo;This card can be readied and spent as if it were a planet card.&rdquo; Learn to Play readies all planet cards at the end of the agenda phase, so The Triad is readied then.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>
</article>
